\PYG{+w}{  }\PYG{n+nx}{idea}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The instrument measures the Xenon lamp through a reference channel and compensates for it. In 155 runs from 2022–2026 the value stayed within ±1 \PYGZpc{}, so it shows regulation, not lamp ageing. Lamp hours and intensity \PYGZpc{} are only in Tools → Instruments (manual p. 208).\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}
\PYG{+w}{  }\PYG{n+nx}{reading}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}Stable = the lamp is still inside the range the instrument can compensate. A step or a point outside the limits = lamp, light guide or reference\PYGZhy{}sensor fault; check the lamp intensity \PYGZpc{} in the instrument software.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
