\PYG{+w}{  }\PYG{k+kd}{const}\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{X}\PYG{o}{=}\PYG{n+nx}{mean}\PYG{p}{(}\PYG{n+nx}{ph}\PYG{p}{.}\PYG{n+nx}{map}\PYG{p}{(}\PYG{n+nx}{g}\PYG{p}{=\PYGZgt{}}\PYG{n+nx}{g}\PYG{p}{.}\PYG{n+nx}{mean}\PYG{p}{)),}\PYG{n+nx}{S}\PYG{o}{=}\PYG{n+nx}{mean}\PYG{p}{(}\PYG{n+nx}{ph}\PYG{p}{.}\PYG{n+nx}{map}\PYG{p}{(}\PYG{n+nx}{g}\PYG{p}{=\PYGZgt{}}\PYG{n+nx}{g}\PYG{p}{.}\PYG{n+nx}{sd}\PYG{p}{).}\PYG{n+nx}{filter}\PYG{p}{(}\PYG{n+nb}{Number}\PYG{p}{.}\PYG{n+nb}{isFinite}\PYG{p}{));}
\PYG{+w}{  }\PYG{c+cm}{/* three\PYGZhy{}way chart (Wheeler): the limits of the run means use the larger of the within\PYGZhy{}run spread (A3·S̄) and the}
\PYG{c+cm}{     run\PYGZhy{}to\PYGZhy{}run moving range of the means (MR̄/1.128). With many readings per run the within\PYGZhy{}run S alone gives limits}
\PYG{c+cm}{     far narrower than the normal day\PYGZhy{}to\PYGZhy{}day variation and would flag almost every run. */}
\PYG{+w}{  }\PYG{k+kd}{const}\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{mr}\PYG{o}{=}\PYG{n+nx}{ph}\PYG{p}{.}\PYG{n+nx}{slice}\PYG{p}{(}\PYG{l+m+mf}{1}\PYG{p}{).}\PYG{n+nx}{map}\PYG{p}{((}\PYG{n+nx}{g}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{i}\PYG{p}{)=\PYGZgt{}}\PYG{n+nb}{Math}\PYG{p}{.}\PYG{n+nx}{abs}\PYG{p}{(}\PYG{n+nx}{g}\PYG{p}{.}\PYG{n+nx}{mean}\PYG{o}{\PYGZhy{}}\PYG{n+nx}{ph}\PYG{p}{[}\PYG{n+nx}{i}\PYG{p}{].}\PYG{n+nx}{mean}\PYG{p}{)),}\PYG{n+nx}{sigB}\PYG{o}{=}\PYG{n+nx}{mr}\PYG{p}{.}\PYG{n+nx}{length}\PYG{o}{?}\PYG{n+nx}{mean}\PYG{p}{(}\PYG{n+nx}{mr}\PYG{p}{)}\PYG{o}{/}\PYG{l+m+mf}{1.128}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+m+mf}{0}\PYG{p}{;}
\PYG{+w}{  }\PYG{k}{return}\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{cl}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{n+nx}{X}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{sbar}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{n+nx}{S}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{sigB}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{pts}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{n+nx}{groups}\PYG{p}{.}\PYG{n+nx}{map}\PYG{p}{(}\PYG{n+nx}{g}\PYG{p}{=\PYGZgt{}\PYGZob{}}\PYG{k}{if}\PYG{p}{(}\PYG{o}{!}\PYG{n+nx}{g}\PYG{o}{||!}\PYG{n+nb}{Number}\PYG{p}{.}\PYG{n+nb}{isFinite}\PYG{p}{(}\PYG{n+nx}{g}\PYG{p}{.}\PYG{n+nx}{mean}\PYG{p}{))}\PYG{k}{return}\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{y}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{k+kc}{NaN}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{cl}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{n+nx}{X}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{flags}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{[]\PYGZcb{};}
\PYG{+w}{    }\PYG{k+kd}{const}\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{n}\PYG{o}{=}\PYG{n+nb}{Math}\PYG{p}{.}\PYG{n+nx}{max}\PYG{p}{(}\PYG{l+m+mf}{2}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{g}\PYG{p}{.}\PYG{n+nx}{n}\PYG{o}{||}\PYG{l+m+mf}{2}\PYG{p}{),}\PYG{n+nx}{c4}\PYG{o}{=}\PYG{n+nx}{CC\PYGZus{}C4}\PYG{p}{(}\PYG{n+nx}{n}\PYG{p}{),}\PYG{n+nx}{A3}\PYG{o}{=}\PYG{l+m+mf}{3}\PYG{o}{/}\PYG{p}{(}\PYG{n+nx}{c4}\PYG{o}{*}\PYG{n+nb}{Math}\PYG{p}{.}\PYG{n+nx}{sqrt}\PYG{p}{(}\PYG{n+nx}{n}\PYG{p}{)),}\PYG{n+nx}{B4}\PYG{o}{=}\PYG{l+m+mf}{1}\PYG{o}{+}\PYG{l+m+mf}{3}\PYG{o}{*}\PYG{n+nb}{Math}\PYG{p}{.}\PYG{n+nx}{sqrt}\PYG{p}{(}\PYG{l+m+mf}{1}\PYG{o}{\PYGZhy{}}\PYG{n+nx}{c4}\PYG{o}{*}\PYG{n+nx}{c4}\PYG{p}{)}\PYG{o}{/}\PYG{n+nx}{c4}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{w}\PYG{o}{=}\PYG{n+nb}{Math}\PYG{p}{.}\PYG{n+nx}{max}\PYG{p}{(}\PYG{n+nx}{A3}\PYG{o}{*}\PYG{n+nx}{S}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{l+m+mf}{3}\PYG{o}{*}\PYG{n+nx}{sigB}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{l+m+mf}{1.5}\PYG{o}{*}\PYG{p}{(}\PYG{n+nx}{cfg}\PYG{p}{.}\PYG{n+nx}{res}\PYG{o}{||}\PYG{l+m+mf}{0}\PYG{p}{));}
\PYG{+w}{    }\PYG{k+kd}{const}\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{f}\PYG{o}{=}\PYG{p}{[];}\PYG{k}{if}\PYG{p}{(}\PYG{n+nb}{Math}\PYG{p}{.}\PYG{n+nx}{abs}\PYG{p}{(}\PYG{n+nx}{g}\PYG{p}{.}\PYG{n+nx}{mean}\PYG{o}{\PYGZhy{}}\PYG{n+nx}{X}\PYG{p}{)}\PYG{o}{\PYGZgt{}}\PYG{n+nx}{w}\PYG{p}{)}\PYG{n+nx}{f}\PYG{p}{.}\PYG{n+nx}{push}\PYG{p}{(}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}mean beyond limit\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{);}\PYG{k}{if}\PYG{p}{(}\PYG{n+nx}{g}\PYG{p}{.}\PYG{n+nx}{sd}\PYG{o}{\PYGZgt{}}\PYG{n+nx}{B4}\PYG{o}{*}\PYG{n+nx}{S}\PYG{p}{)}\PYG{n+nx}{f}\PYG{p}{.}\PYG{n+nx}{push}\PYG{p}{(}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}spread (S) beyond limit\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{);}
\PYG{+w}{    }\PYG{k}{return}\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{y}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{n+nx}{g}\PYG{p}{.}\PYG{n+nx}{mean}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{s}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{n+nx}{g}\PYG{p}{.}\PYG{n+nx}{sd}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{cl}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{n+nx}{X}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{ucl}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{n+nx}{X}\PYG{o}{+}\PYG{n+nx}{w}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{lcl}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{n+nx}{X}\PYG{o}{\PYGZhy{}}\PYG{n+nx}{w}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{sUcl}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{n+nx}{B4}\PYG{o}{*}\PYG{n+nx}{S}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{flags}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{n+nx}{f}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{};\PYGZcb{})\PYGZcb{};}
\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{}}
\PYG{k+kd}{function}\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{ccFunnel}\PYG{p}{(}\PYG{n+nx}{rows}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{metric}\PYG{p}{)\PYGZob{}}\PYG{+w}{            }\PYG{c+c1}{// one point per operator}
\PYG{+w}{  }\PYG{k+kd}{const}\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{by}\PYG{o}{=}\PYG{n+nx}{byKey}\PYG{p}{(}\PYG{n+nx}{rows}\PYG{p}{.}\PYG{n+nx}{filter}\PYG{p}{(}\PYG{n+nx}{r}\PYG{p}{=\PYGZgt{}}\PYG{n+nx}{r}\PYG{p}{.}\PYG{n+nx}{m}\PYG{p}{[}\PYG{n+nx}{metric}\PYG{p}{]}\PYG{o}{\PYGZam{}\PYGZam{}}\PYG{n+nx}{r}\PYG{p}{.}\PYG{n+nx}{m}\PYG{p}{[}\PYG{n+nx}{metric}\PYG{p}{].}\PYG{n+nx}{n}\PYG{p}{),}\PYG{n+nx}{r}\PYG{p}{=\PYGZgt{}}\PYG{n+nx}{r}\PYG{p}{.}\PYG{n+nx}{operator}\PYG{o}{||}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}(not recorded)\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{);}
\PYG{+w}{  }\PYG{k+kd}{const}\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{tot}\PYG{o}{=}\PYG{p}{[...}\PYG{n+nx}{by}\PYG{p}{.}\PYG{n+nx}{values}\PYG{p}{()].}\PYG{n+nx}{flat}\PYG{p}{(),}\PYG{n+nx}{p0}\PYG{o}{=}\PYG{n+nx}{tot}\PYG{p}{.}\PYG{n+nx}{reduce}\PYG{p}{((}\PYG{n+nx}{s}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{r}\PYG{p}{)=\PYGZgt{}}\PYG{n+nx}{s}\PYG{o}{+}\PYG{n+nx}{r}\PYG{p}{.}\PYG{n+nx}{m}\PYG{p}{[}\PYG{n+nx}{metric}\PYG{p}{].}\PYG{n+nx}{bad}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{l+m+mf}{0}\PYG{p}{)}\PYG{o}{/}\PYG{p}{(}\PYG{n+nx}{tot}\PYG{p}{.}\PYG{n+nx}{reduce}\PYG{p}{((}\PYG{n+nx}{s}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{r}\PYG{p}{)=\PYGZgt{}}\PYG{n+nx}{s}\PYG{o}{+}\PYG{n+nx}{r}\PYG{p}{.}\PYG{n+nx}{m}\PYG{p}{[}\PYG{n+nx}{metric}\PYG{p}{].}\PYG{n+nx}{n}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{l+m+mf}{0}\PYG{p}{)}\PYG{o}{||}\PYG{l+m+mf}{1}\PYG{p}{);}
\PYG{+w}{  }\PYG{k}{return}\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{p0}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{pts}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{[...}\PYG{n+nx}{by}\PYG{p}{].}\PYG{n+nx}{map}\PYG{p}{(([}\PYG{n+nx}{op}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{rs}\PYG{p}{])=\PYGZgt{}\PYGZob{}}\PYG{k+kd}{const}\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{b}\PYG{o}{=}\PYG{n+nx}{rs}\PYG{p}{.}\PYG{n+nx}{reduce}\PYG{p}{((}\PYG{n+nx}{s}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{r}\PYG{p}{)=\PYGZgt{}}\PYG{n+nx}{s}\PYG{o}{+}\PYG{n+nx}{r}\PYG{p}{.}\PYG{n+nx}{m}\PYG{p}{[}\PYG{n+nx}{metric}\PYG{p}{].}\PYG{n+nx}{bad}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{l+m+mf}{0}\PYG{p}{),}\PYG{n+nx}{n}\PYG{o}{=}\PYG{n+nx}{rs}\PYG{p}{.}\PYG{n+nx}{reduce}\PYG{p}{((}\PYG{n+nx}{s}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{r}\PYG{p}{)=\PYGZgt{}}\PYG{n+nx}{s}\PYG{o}{+}\PYG{n+nx}{r}\PYG{p}{.}\PYG{n+nx}{m}\PYG{p}{[}\PYG{n+nx}{metric}\PYG{p}{].}\PYG{n+nx}{n}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{l+m+mf}{0}\PYG{p}{),}\PYG{n+nx}{y}\PYG{o}{=}\PYG{n+nx}{b}\PYG{o}{/}\PYG{n+nx}{n}\PYG{p}{;}
\PYG{+w}{    }\PYG{k+kd}{const}\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{u95}\PYG{o}{=}\PYG{n+nx}{p0}\PYG{o}{+}\PYG{l+m+mf}{1.96}\PYG{o}{*}\PYG{n+nb}{Math}\PYG{p}{.}\PYG{n+nx}{sqrt}\PYG{p}{(}\PYG{n+nx}{p0}\PYG{o}{*}\PYG{p}{(}\PYG{l+m+mf}{1}\PYG{o}{\PYGZhy{}}\PYG{n+nx}{p0}\PYG{p}{)}\PYG{o}{/}\PYG{n+nx}{n}\PYG{p}{),}\PYG{n+nx}{u998}\PYG{o}{=}\PYG{n+nx}{p0}\PYG{o}{+}\PYG{l+m+mf}{3.09}\PYG{o}{*}\PYG{n+nb}{Math}\PYG{p}{.}\PYG{n+nx}{sqrt}\PYG{p}{(}\PYG{n+nx}{p0}\PYG{o}{*}\PYG{p}{(}\PYG{l+m+mf}{1}\PYG{o}{\PYGZhy{}}\PYG{n+nx}{p0}\PYG{p}{)}\PYG{o}{/}\PYG{n+nx}{n}\PYG{p}{);}
\PYG{+w}{    }\PYG{k}{return}\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{operator}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{n+nx}{op}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{n}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{bad}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{n+nx}{b}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{y}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{u95}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{u998}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{flags}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{n+nx}{y}\PYG{o}{\PYGZgt{}}\PYG{n+nx}{u998}\PYG{o}{?}\PYG{p}{[}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}outside 99.8 \PYGZpc{}\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{]}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{n+nx}{y}\PYG{o}{\PYGZgt{}}\PYG{n+nx}{u95}\PYG{o}{?}\PYG{p}{[}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}outside 95 \PYGZpc{}\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{]}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{[]\PYGZcb{};\PYGZcb{})\PYGZcb{};}
\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{}}

\PYG{c+cm}{/* what a result below / above the limits means, per chart (shown on the chart page and in the alarm table) */}
\PYG{k+kd}{const}\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{CC\PYGZus{}LIMIT\PYGZus{}TEXT}\PYG{o}{=}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{heat\PYGZus{}rate}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}Heating is slower than usual. A single low run: plate not seated, wrong plate type, blocked air vents or a warm room that day. A slow fall over many runs: Peltier elements or thermal paste ageing — plan a thermal service before the specification (4.3 °C/s on the LightCycler) is reached.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}Heating is faster than usual. Usually harmless: after a service, a new block or a firmware change. If isolated, check the run used the same protocol and plate; very fast ramps with a larger overshoot can stress samples.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{cool\PYGZus{}rate}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}Cooling is slower than usual: the heat sink is not getting rid of heat. First clean the fan filters and check that all fans run and the vents are free; then check room temperature. If cooling keeps falling while heating stays normal after cleaning, the Peltier/heat\PYGZhy{}sink contact needs service.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}Cooling is faster than usual. Typical after cleaning the filters, a fan replacement or a service, or in a cooler room. Note the event and, if it was a service, start a new baseline on that date.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{overshoot}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The block overshoots less than it used to (CUSUM drifting down). The temperature controller or the sensor calibration has changed — typical after a service or recalibration. Check that the reading temperature (B\PYGZhy{}H4) did not shift at the same time.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The block overshoots more than it used to (CUSUM drifting up). The controller is compensating for a slower block, or the sensor is ageing. Samples briefly see higher temperatures; check heating rate (B\PYGZhy{}H1) and plan a temperature verification.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{settling}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The block reaches a stable temperature faster than usual. Harmless in itself; if it coincides with a step in overshoot and offset, the controller was re\PYGZhy{}tuned or recalibrated (start a new baseline).\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The block needs longer to settle. With normal ramp rates: control tuning or sensor lag. With slower ramps as well: thermal ageing. Long settling shortens the real hold time at the setpoint and can lower efficiency.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{transition}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The block moves between these two temperatures faster than usual: after a service, a cleaned fan filter or a cooler room. Harmless; if it coincides with a step in overshoot or offset, start a new baseline on the service date.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The block needs longer to move between these two temperatures, so every cycle spends less time at the programmed hold. A cooling transition (e.g. 95 → 60 °C) getting longer = heat removal (clean fan filters, check fans, room temperature); heating transitions getting longer = Peltier ageing. Samples spend more time at intermediate temperatures, which can favour non\PYGZhy{}specific annealing.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{hold\PYGZus{}temp}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}At the moment of reading the block is colder than usual compared with the setpoint (more negative offset). Real sample temperature is lower: annealing becomes less stringent. Check cooling (B\PYGZhy{}H2) and room temperature; persistent change needs a temperature verification plate or recalibration. S above its limit = temperature not stable during the reading.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}At the moment of reading the block is warmer than usual compared with the setpoint. Real sample temperature is higher: annealing is more stringent and weakly binding probes can lose signal. Typical after a recalibration (start a new baseline); otherwise verify with a temperature plate. S above its limit = temperature not stable during the reading.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{zone\PYGZus{}spread}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The six block zones agree better than usual. Harmless; typical after a block service or recalibration.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The block zones disagree more than usual: wells in different parts of the plate see different temperatures, which shows up as edge or row/column Cq patterns (B\PYGZhy{}O3). Check plate seating and seal; if it persists or exceeds 1.5 °C, request a block uniformity service.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{heatsink\PYGZus{}max}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The heat sink stays cooler than usual: cooler room or cleaned fans/filters. Harmless.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The heat sink runs hotter than usual: airflow is reduced (dust in filters, failing fan, instrument too close to a wall) or the room is warm. Expect slower cooling (B\PYGZhy{}H2). Clean filters, check fans and clearance.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{cover\PYGZus{}temp}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The heated cover is colder than its setpoint: condensation can form under the seal and change reaction volumes. Check that the cover heats and that the run was not started with the cover disabled; recurring = cover heater service.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The heated cover is warmer than its setpoint: control fault or sensor error. Seals can deform; report to service if repeated.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{lamp\PYGZus{}ref}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The lamp reference reading is lower than usual: less light reaches the reference sensor. Lamp near the end of its range, light guide or filter dirty, or the lamp was not warmed up. Check lamp intensity \PYGZpc{} and hours in Tools → Instruments.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The lamp reference reading is higher than usual: typically a new lamp or a service (start a new baseline). Otherwise a reference\PYGZhy{}sensor fault; check the lamp intensity \PYGZpc{} in the instrument software.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{lamp\PYGZus{}drift}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}Lamp output falls during the run more than usual: the lamp is unstable (ageing) or was not warmed up. Late\PYGZhy{}cycle fluorescence may be under\PYGZhy{}reported; check the lamp.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}Lamp output rises during the run more than usual: the lamp was still warming up at the start, or it flickers. Early\PYGZhy{}cycle baselines can be affected; allow warm\PYGZhy{}up and check the lamp.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{led\PYGZus{}current}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The LED is driven with less current than usual: either the LED is brighter than expected (after a service) or the driver is limiting. Check that signal levels (A\PYGZhy{}H3) did not drop.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The LED needs more current than usual to give the same light: normal LED ageing. The trend line forecasts when the driver will reach its limit — plan an optics service before that.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{led\PYGZus{}junction}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The LED runs cooler than usual: cooler room or improved airflow. Harmless.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The LED runs hotter than usual: reduced cooling of the optics (fans, filters, room temperature) or higher drive current (B\PYGZhy{}H10). Heat shortens LED life and can shift its colour; check airflow.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{exposure}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}Shorter exposures than usual: the signal is brighter (more template, new reagent lot, higher probe concentration) or the light source is stronger after a service. Check for saturation (B\PYGZhy{}H12).\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}Longer exposures than usual: the instrument is compensating for weak light — weaker probe or dye, wrong plate or seal, dirty optics, or an ageing lamp/LED. If it keeps rising over many runs, service the optics.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{saturation}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}Fewer saturated images than usual: normal.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}More well images are saturated: signal too strong for the camera (too much template or dye, wrong exposure settings, reflective plate). Saturated wells give wrong curve shapes and Cq; dilute samples or check the plate type.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{calib\PYGZus{}uniformity}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The new uniformity calibration shows the plate edges relatively darker than before: optics or illumination changed. Check that the calibration was done with the correct plate, and watch for edge effects in the results.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The new uniformity calibration shows the edges relatively brighter than before: optics or illumination changed, or the calibration plate differed. Confirm with a repeat calibration before accepting it.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{calib\PYGZus{}background}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The background calibration offset is lower than before: cleaner block or new calibration plate. Harmless.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The background calibration offset is higher: contamination (fluorescent residue) on the block or optics, or a light leak. Clean the block, repeat the background calibration.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{calib\PYGZus{}roi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The well spots found by the ROI calibration are smaller than before: focus or alignment changed. Wells may be read off\PYGZhy{}centre; repeat the ROI calibration.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The well spots are larger than before: focus or alignment changed, or a different plate type was used for calibration. Repeat the ROI calibration with the correct plate.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{wheel\PYGZus{}ms}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}Filter\PYGZhy{}wheel moves are faster than usual: typical after a motor service or firmware change. Harmless.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}Filter\PYGZhy{}wheel moves are slower: friction in the bearing, a weakening motor or dust. The wheel may start to miss positions (B\PYGZhy{}H15). Plan a service if the rise continues.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{wheel\PYGZus{}slow}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}Fewer slow moves than usual: normal.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}More filter\PYGZhy{}wheel moves take longer than 500 ms: mechanical wear or intermittent motor problems, often before the median (B\PYGZhy{}H14) changes. Plan a service.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{encoder}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The filter\PYGZhy{}wheel position offset stepped down: the wheel slipped, was re\PYGZhy{}homed or serviced. Wrong filter positions change the signal in every channel; check the dye calibration if unexplained.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The filter\PYGZhy{}wheel position offset stepped up: the wheel slipped, was re\PYGZhy{}homed or serviced. Check the dye calibration if unexplained.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{cam\PYGZus{}overhead}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}Camera readout is faster than usual: firmware or controller change. Harmless.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}Camera readout takes longer than usual. A jump points to the camera or its connection; a slow rise, together with the software charts (B\PYGZhy{}S1–S4), points to the embedded computer slowing down.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{chan\PYGZus{}switch}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}Switching between channels is faster than usual: firmware or mechanical change. Harmless, but note it.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}Switching between channels is slower: filter wheels, the camera readout or the instrument computer are slowing down. The manual allows \PYGZlt{} 0.65 s for the filter switch; if the rise continues, plan a service.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{cover\PYGZus{}down}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The cover lowers faster than usual: typical after lubrication or a drive service. Harmless.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The cover takes longer to lower: the drive mechanism is wearing or needs lubrication, or something obstructs it (tall plate, misplaced adapter). The trend forecasts when the drive will reach its limit.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{cover\PYGZus{}up}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The cover rises faster than usual: harmless.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The cover takes longer to rise: drive wear or the cover sticking to the seal. Check the seal type and the drive.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{bg\PYGZus{}median}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}Background fluorescence is lower than usual: less dye or probe in the wells, a different plate or seal, less volume, or weaker excitation. Check reagent preparation and the exposure chart (B\PYGZhy{}H11).\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}Background fluorescence is higher than usual: more probe or a degraded probe (free dye), fluorescent contamination, a different plate type, or a light leak. Check the reagent lot and plate type.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{plateau\PYGZus{}median}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}End\PYGZhy{}point fluorescence is lower than usual: weaker amplification (inhibition, degraded reagents, less template) or weaker optics. If the positive\PYGZhy{}control Cq is normal, suspect the probe or the optics.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}End\PYGZhy{}point fluorescence is higher than usual: more template or probe, a new reagent lot, or a brighter light source after service. Check for saturation (B\PYGZhy{}H12).\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{run\PYGZus{}minutes}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The run finished faster than usual for this protocol: the run was stopped early or cycles were skipped. Check the run was complete before accepting results.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The run took longer than usual for this protocol: slower ramps (B\PYGZhy{}H1/B\PYGZhy{}H2), longer exposures (B\PYGZhy{}H11), a pause, or the instrument computer slowing. Look at those charts for the same run.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{cmd\PYGZus{}rt}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The instrument answers the PC faster than usual: harmless (firmware or PC change).\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The instrument answers the PC more slowly: embedded computer busy or ageing, storage slow, or network/USB problems. Rising together with B\PYGZhy{}S2/B\PYGZhy{}S3 = instrument computer; alone = PC or connection.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{tick\PYGZus{}late}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The 1\PYGZhy{}s timer fires more punctually than usual: harmless.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The 1\PYGZhy{}s timer fires late: the embedded computer is overloaded or its storage is slow. Timing of steps and readings can drift; if it keeps rising, request a vendor check of the instrument computer.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{catch\PYGZus{}up}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The scheduler falls behind less often: normal.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The task scheduler falls behind more often: the instrument computer cannot keep up. Watch reply time (B\PYGZhy{}S1) and processing delay (B\PYGZhy{}S3); a vendor check may be needed.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{img\PYGZus{}proc}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}Images are processed sooner than usual: harmless.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}Images wait longer before processing: the instrument computer is busy, storage is slow or nearly full. Clear old data on the instrument; persistent rise = vendor check.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{roi\PYGZus{}ms}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}Image analysis is faster than usual: harmless (firmware update).\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}Image analysis takes longer: the instrument computer is slowing (storage, memory) or the plate layout is heavier (more wells, more dyes). Compare with runs of the same plate layout.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{runtime\PYGZus{}err}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The run finished earlier than the software predicted: the prediction model changed, or the run was shortened. Check that the run completed.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The run took longer than the software predicted: slower ramps, longer exposures or computer delays add up. Look at the thermal and software charts for the same run.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{handoff\PYGZus{}min}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}Data were packed for the PC faster than usual: harmless.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}Data were packed long after the run ended: the file was saved or transferred late (PC off, network down, run left on the instrument). For forensic review, check that nothing was changed in between.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{log\PYGZus{}errors}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}Fewer command errors than usual: normal.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}More command errors than usual: communication problems between PC and instrument, a firmware/software mismatch or a hardware fault. Read the instrument log for the run and contact service if it repeats.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{cycle\PYGZus{}sd}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}Cycles are more regular than usual: harmless.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}Cycle length varies more within the run: the instrument paused, waited for the computer, or thermal steps took variable time. Irregular cycles can change Cq; check the run timeline graph.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{templog\PYGZus{}late}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}Fewer late temperature\PYGZhy{}log intervals: normal.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}More temperature\PYGZhy{}log intervals exceed 500 ms: the control loop is being interrupted — computer overload or a communication problem. Temperature control may be affected; check the thermal charts.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{invalid\PYGZus{}acq}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}Fewer invalid readings: normal.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}More fluorescence readings are marked invalid by the instrument: optics, lamp or camera problems, or the signal was out of range. Check exposure (B\PYGZhy{}H11) and lamp (B\PYGZhy{}H8); affected wells may need repeating.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{ct\PYGZus{}mismatch}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}Fewer wells whose stored Ct cannot be reproduced: normal.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}More wells have a stored Ct that the page cannot reproduce from the stored data: manual threshold or baseline changes, a software version change, or data edited after analysis. Check the analysis settings and the audit trail.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{edit\PYGZus{}delay}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}Results were finalised sooner after the run than usual: good practice.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The file was last changed much later than usual after the run: late analysis, or re\PYGZhy{}analysis long after the run. For forensic review, check who changed what and why (audit trail).\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{findings}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}Fewer forensic findings than usual: normal.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}More forensic findings than usual for one run: open the Quality \PYGZam{} forensic review tab for this run and resolve each finding before accepting the results.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{pc\PYGZus{}cq}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The positive control amplified earlier than its range: more control template (new lot, pipetting), contamination, or a more efficient reaction. Westgard rules decide whether the run is rejected; check the control lot and pipetting.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The positive control amplified later than its range: degraded control or reagents, inhibition, pipetting error, or weaker optics. A trend over several runs points to reagent storage or lot ageing; a single point to the run itself.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{pc\PYGZus{}amplitude}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The probe signal of the control is weaker than usual: probe degradation (light, freeze–thaw), a new lot with less signal, wrong dye/quencher setup or weaker optics. Weak signal makes Cq calls less reliable; check reagent storage and lot.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The probe signal is stronger than usual: a new lot, higher probe concentration or a stronger light source. Check for saturation (B\PYGZhy{}H12) and that thresholds still suit the curves.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{rox\PYGZus{}level}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The passive reference (ROX) is lower than usual: less master mix dispensed, a master mix without or with less ROX, or wrong dye settings. Normalised results may be noisier; check the master mix and pipetting.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The passive reference is higher than usual: more volume, a master mix with more ROX, or evaporation concentrating the wells. Check the master mix type and the seal.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{efficiency}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}PCR efficiency is lower than usual (below 90 \PYGZpc{} is outside MIQE): inhibition, degraded reagents, poor primer/probe, or wrong dilutions of the standards. Quantities will be biased; repeat the standard curve.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}PCR efficiency is higher than usual (above 110 \PYGZpc{} is outside MIQE): usually a pipetting or dilution error in the standards, inhibition in the concentrated standards, or primer\PYGZhy{}dimers. Repeat the dilution series.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{ntc\PYGZus{}rate}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}Fewer positive negative controls than usual: normal.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}More no\PYGZhy{}template controls show a Cq: contamination (reagents, pipettes, bench, amplicon carry\PYGZhy{}over) or probe degradation giving false signal. Stop, decontaminate, replace reagents; results of affected runs need review.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{ic\PYGZus{}shift}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The internal control in samples amplifies earlier than the configured fixed reference Cq. Check control input, assay settings and reference applicability before attributing a cause.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The internal control in samples is delayed: inhibition from the sample matrix or extraction carry\PYGZhy{}over (ethanol, salts), or extraction losses. Affected samples may give false negatives; re\PYGZhy{}extract or dilute.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{low\PYGZus{}conf}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}Fewer low\PYGZhy{}confidence Cq calls: normal.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}More wells have low Cq confidence: noisy or odd\PYGZhy{}shaped curves from weak probes, bubbles, evaporation or low template. Review the flagged curves before reporting.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{late\PYGZus{}rate}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}Fewer results in the late or stochastic zone: normal.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}More results fall in the late\PYGZhy{}signal or stochastic zone: low template amounts, inhibition, degraded samples or less sensitive reagents. These results are less reliable; follow the SOP for repeats.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{rep\PYGZus{}sd}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}Replicates agree better than usual: good pipetting. Harmless.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}Replicates agree less than usual: pipetting imprecision (technique, uncalibrated pipette, bubbles), poor mixing or bad plate sealing. Check the pipette calibration and retrain if it is linked to one operator.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{rox\PYGZus{}cv}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The dispensed volume is more even than usual: good. Harmless.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}Dispensed volumes vary more across the plate: pipetting technique, a pipette out of calibration or a failing multichannel channel. Check the pipettes and the operator\PYGZsq{}s technique.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{rowcol}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}(A lower value is always good — no action.)\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}One plate row or column differs from the rest: a blocked or faulty multichannel tip, a pipetting order error, or a block zone problem (B\PYGZhy{}H5). Look at the plate heat map to see which row or column.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{ntc\PYGZus{}op}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}(Below the funnel is not possible for a rate — no action.)\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}This operator\PYGZsq{}s NTC positive rate is higher than expected for their workload: outside 95 \PYGZpc{} = watch, outside 99.8 \PYGZpc{} = investigate the operator\PYGZsq{}s contamination\PYGZhy{}control technique (gloves, tips, workflow) and offer retraining.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{action\PYGZus{}op}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}(Below the funnel is not possible for a rate — no action.)\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}This operator gets more repeats, inconclusive or invalid results than expected for their workload: check sample handling, pipetting and SOP understanding; use it for training, not ranking.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{manual\PYGZus{}rate}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}Fewer manual changes than usual: normal.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}More settings or wells were changed by hand (threshold, baseline, omitted wells, manual calls): the automatic analysis does not suit the data, or results were adjusted. Each change should be justified in the record.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{n+nx}{call\PYGZus{}disagree}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}Fewer calls disagree with the SOP: normal.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}More stored calls disagree with the SOP rules: calls were made by hand, the software settings differ from the SOP, or the SOP profile loaded in the page is not the one in use. Review each disagreement.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{},}
\PYG{+w}{  }\PYG{n+nx}{copied}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n+nx}{lo}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}(Zero is the expected value.)\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}\PYG{n+nx}{hi}\PYG{o}{:}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}Identical curves or Cq values were found where independent data are expected: copied or duplicated data. This is a forensic finding — secure the original files and investigate.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{}\PYGZcb{};}
