\PYG{c+cm}{/* ============================================================}
\PYG{c+cm}{   A2. Sample roles}
\PYG{c+cm}{   \PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}}
\PYG{c+cm}{   The decoder already carries the instrument\PYGZsq{}s own sample type}
\PYG{c+cm}{   (QuantSampleTypeProperty \PYGZhy{}\PYGZgt{} instrRole). That is authoritative when it is set,}
\PYG{c+cm}{   because it is what the operator entered in the Sample Editor. Many routine}
\PYG{c+cm}{   runs leave every well as \PYGZdq{}Unknown\PYGZdq{}, so the sample name is used as a fallback}
\PYG{c+cm}{   \PYGZhy{} and only as a fallback, since a name is a label and a sample type is a}
\PYG{c+cm}{   declaration. Where the two disagree the instrument wins and the disagreement}
\PYG{c+cm}{   is recorded, so it can be reported rather than silently resolved.}
\PYG{c+cm}{   ============================================================ */}
