\PYG{c+cm}{/* ============================================================}
\PYG{c+cm}{   C. Open formats}
\PYG{c+cm}{   \PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}}
\PYG{c+cm}{   Two details here were established by running the target tools rather}
\PYG{c+cm}{   than by reading their documentation, and both are load\PYGZhy{}bearing:}

\PYG{c+cm}{   1. rdmlpython refuses LinRegPCR below RDML 1.4}
\PYG{c+cm}{      (\PYGZdq{}LinRegPCR requires RDML version \PYGZgt{}= 1.4\PYGZdq{}), so 1.4 is written.}
\PYG{c+cm}{   2. It resolves a target\PYGZsq{}s chemistry through the dye table and raises}
\PYG{c+cm}{      KeyError on the target id if the referenced dye was never declared.}
\PYG{c+cm}{      Writing \PYGZlt{}dyeId\PYGZgt{} without a matching \PYGZlt{}dye\PYGZgt{} element therefore produces}
\PYG{c+cm}{      a file that opens, validates and then fails halfway through analysis.}
\PYG{c+cm}{      Every referenced dye is declared.}
\PYG{c+cm}{   ============================================================ */}
