\PYG{l+s+sb}{Files}
\PYG{l+s+sb}{  cq\PYGZus{}values.csv         stored crossing points (Cq / Ct), one row per result; QuantStudio flags, ΔCt, ΔΔCt, RQ}
\PYG{l+s+sb}{  runs\PYGZus{}qc\PYGZus{}forensic\PYGZus{}log.csv   container integrity, control, flag and traceability findings}
\PYG{l+s+sb}{  relative\PYGZus{}quantification.csv  stored ΔΔCt / ratio summaries, if any}
\PYG{l+s+sb}{  multicomponent\PYGZus{}raw.csv  QuantStudio per\PYGZhy{}dye and per\PYGZhy{}filter signal, if any}
\PYG{l+s+sb}{  \PYGZlt{}run\PYGZgt{}/*\PYGZus{}QuantStudio\PYGZus{}export.txt   QuantStudio export layout as text (MAN0010409, chapter 3)}
\PYG{l+s+sb}{  \PYGZlt{}run\PYGZgt{}/*\PYGZus{}QuantStudio\PYGZus{}export.xlsx  the same as a workbook with the software\PYGZsq{}s sheet layout}
\PYG{l+s+sb}{  \PYGZlt{}run\PYGZgt{}/instrument\PYGZus{}records/*.csv  run metadata, integrity, program, channels, calibrations, log}
\PYG{l+s+sb}{  melting\PYGZus{}peaks.csv     melting temperatures, if the run has a Tm analysis}
\PYG{l+s+sb}{  experiment\PYGZus{}settings.csv  every setting read out of the container, with its source}
\PYG{l+s+sb}{  metadata.jsonld       Schema.org/DCAT dataset metadata with PROV\PYGZhy{}O/PAV provenance}
\PYG{l+s+sb}{  checksums.sha256      SHA\PYGZhy{}256 of every component in this open bundle}
\PYG{l+s+sb}{  \PYGZlt{}run\PYGZgt{}/rdml\PYGZus{}data.xml   RDML 1.4 \PYGZhy{} rename to .rdml or zip it to open in RDML tools}
\PYG{l+s+sb}{  \PYGZlt{}run\PYGZgt{}/*\PYGZus{}qpcR\PYGZus{}curves.csv     one wide curve table per analysis, first column \PYGZdq{}Cycles\PYGZdq{}}
\PYG{l+s+sb}{  \PYGZlt{}run\PYGZgt{}/*.rdes.tsv            one long curve table per analysis, one row per cycle}
\PYG{l+s+sb}{  analyse\PYGZus{}with\PYGZus{}qpcR.R         fits the curves in R and compares with stored Cq}
\PYG{l+s+sb}{  analyse\PYGZus{}with\PYGZus{}linregpcr.py   runs LinRegPCR through rdmlpython}

\PYG{l+s+sb}{Two things worth knowing}
\PYG{l+s+sb}{  Keep the original .ixo / .eds alongside this open bundle. It is the provenance anchor;}
\PYG{l+s+sb}{  its SHA\PYGZhy{}256 is recorded above and in metadata.jsonld, but the original vendor}
\PYG{l+s+sb}{  container is not duplicated inside this export.}

\PYG{l+s+sb}{  RDML is written at version 1.4 because rdmlpython refuses to run LinRegPCR on}
\PYG{l+s+sb}{  anything older, and every dye is declared as its own element because it raises}
\PYG{l+s+sb}{  KeyError on a target whose dye is only referenced. Both were found by running}
\PYG{l+s+sb}{  the tool, not by reading the specification.}

\PYG{l+s+sb}{  The values in cq\PYGZus{}values.csv are the instrument\PYGZsq{}s own. Nothing was recomputed.}
\PYG{l+s+sb}{  Where this export disagrees with the instrument software, the file is the}
\PYG{l+s+sb}{  reference \PYGZhy{} please report it. If sample names were pseudonymised, the mapping}
\PYG{l+s+sb}{  is not part of this bundle.}
\PYG{l+s+sb}{`}\PYG{p}{;}
\PYG{p}{\PYGZcb{}}

